# gov_cooldown_v1.tau  --  ZenoDEX governance: per-surface revision COOLDOWN bit (universal)
# MUTABILITY: UPDATABLE (the gate logic; the cooldown length is supplied per call)
# SHAPE: pure hysteresis bit -- distinct from the TIMELOCK (delay between a specific
# proposal and its execution). The cooldown is the minimum spacing between two
# CONSECUTIVE APPLIED revisions of the same surface, killing parameter thrash and
# oscillation games regardless of which proposer is active. Composed (ANDed) by the
# epoch machine alongside the pointwise revision gates.
#
# Inputs:
#   i1 = last_revision_epoch (bv[16]) -- epoch of the last APPLIED revision (committed)
#   i2 = now_epoch           (bv[16]) -- current epoch
#   i3 = cooldown            (bv[16]) -- minimum epochs between applied revisions
# Output:
#   o1 = cooldown_ok (sbf) -- 1 iff now >= last AND now - last >= cooldown
#
# Wrap-safety: the SUBTRACTION-GUARD form (now >= last AND now - last >= cooldown), the
# same wrap-safe shape as the timelock. The naive `now >= last + cooldown` is bypassable
# by bv[16] modular wrap when `last` is near 2^16.

always
  (o1[t]:sbf = 1:sbf <->
    ( (i2[t]:bv[16] >= i1[t]:bv[16])
      && ((i2[t]:bv[16] - i1[t]:bv[16]) >= i3[t]:bv[16])
    )
  ).
